scription":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":21,"created_at":"2025-09-20T19:23:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T00:46:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested in Godot 4.5 stable vs Godot 4.4 stable. (4.4.1 not tested.)\n\n### System information\n\n2019 MBP, Mac OS 15.6.1, Intel CPU, Intel UHD Graphics 630\n\n### Issue description\n\n- Triangle edges have an \"outline\" on metallic (\"shiny\") surfaces.\n- Smooth shading seems require to cause the issue.\n- Setting Roughness all the way up makes them go away but that's removes the metallic effect.\n- The first frame of the running game does not have the problem.\n- The issue is present in 4.5 but not 4.4. (4.4.1 was not tested.)\n\n<img width=\"156\" height=\"206\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5d59f81-f328-4921-b6f1-0e2589aad4ae\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new file in Blender and press A then X then D to safely annihilate the default cube.\n- Press Shift + A and create a new Sphere Mesh.\n- Right click on the Mesh and select Shade Smooth.\n- Add a new Material.\n- Set Metallic to 0.5.\n- Set Roughness to 0.0.\n- Export the file and a GLB/GLTF.\n- Open Godot 4.5 stable.\n- Make a new 3D Scene and Place the GLB in the node tree.\n- You should immediately see the issue in 3D preview area, and when you run the Scene.\n\nIf you add the same GLB to Godot 4.4 stable, you will not see the issue.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[vector_tearing_issue_2025-09-20_15-15-35.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22445271/vector_tearing_issue_2025-09-20_15-15-35.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110732/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110732/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}